! mcp_bootstrap_p132.strap -- the TAIL OF THE INDICATOR-FIX TABLE and
! the common PREFIX routine YPREFX, printed page 132.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.139, header READ and not assumed:
! "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID ED000050
!  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  132", and the header's own
! "LOCATION 216440" field names the page's first word.
!
! FIFTY LINES, ALL OF THEM CODE OR DATA.  No comment cards, no
! heading box, no DRZ.  The card-serial column runs ED000050
! (line 1) to ED000099 (line 50) -- fifty consecutive serials for
! fifty lines, ONE CARD PER LINE, counted off the serial column, so
! nothing fell off the top or the bottom of the render.  (The volume
! survey OCR of this page read 35 rows over 216441..216474; that is
! a window, not the page.  See THE SURVEY, below.)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN IS READ TWICE AND THE BACKWARD JOIN IS NOT MEASURED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE PAGE PRINTS NO SLC. <<<  216440.40 is line 1's own
! LOCATION, and the page header's "LOCATION 216440" prints the same
! word independently, so the SLC below is a READING of two printed
! fields and not a guess.  What it is NOT is a test of contiguity
! with printed p.131: pp.129-131 are not transcribed, so there is no
! landed deck to join to, and a hard SLC asserts its value rather
! than checking it (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "A HARD SLC
! CANNOT DISAGREE WITH THE ARRIVING COUNTER").
!
! The backward join is nevertheless CONSISTENT on an independent
! reading: docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt carries printed p.131's
! row "216440.C0  216457.40 80   YFXAD  SIC,YPREL", a HALF word at
! 216440.00, which leaves the counter at exactly 216440.40 -- this
! page's line 1.  The OCR is a cross-check and never a source, so
! that is consistency, not measurement.  When p.131 lands, compare
! by hand.
!
! THE FORWARD JOIN HAS TWO WITNESSES THAT AGREE.  The counter leaves
! line 50 at 216500.40 (line 50 is a half word at 216500.00).  The
! same OCR reads printed p.133's line 1 as "216500.40  215006.02 30
! YMCPPE  LV,$1,SYCOCH", which is that half word; and line 41 of
! THIS page, "BB1,SL,YMCPPE", branches to 216500.40.  The deck's own
! YMCPPE SYN is that address, so line 41's !CHECK is a test of the
! forward join as well as of the row.
!
! TAIL SCOPE.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! origin here and pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the TAIL,(2)G block that printed
! p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed, so a name here may
! legitimately repeat a name from pp.2-98 at a different address.
! Nothing on this page does: every name it DEFINES is Y-prefixed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This is the end of MCP's INDICATOR-FIX table and the routine every
! entry of it calls.
!
! Lines 1-11  the last three entries of a table that begins on
!             printed p.131.  Each entry is four rows:
!
!                 YFXxxx  SIC,YPREL            store the return IC
!                         B,YPREFX             into YPREL's address
!                         (AX)DD(BU,32), nn X  the indicator's
!                         (IQSX)DD(BU,32),nn X initials, twice
!
!             Line 1 is the "B,YPREFX" of p.131's last entry, whose
!             label (YFXAD, per the volume OCR) is on that page; its
!             two data rows are lines 2 and 3 here.  Lines 4-7 are
!             YFXUSA and lines 8-11 are YFXDS.
!
!             THE TWO DATA ROWS ARE THE SAME TEXT IN TWO CHARACTER
!             SETS -- "(AX)" is Reference Manual p.166's 48 Character
!             Set and "(IQSX)" its 89 Character Set -- and together
!             they make the 64 bits that line 27's "L(BU),$" loads.
!             Lines 28 and 29 then store the two halves to two
!             different places (YPPEM+.8, the printed message, and
!             YMCPIN).
!
! Lines 12-26 YPREFX.  Line 12 tests S L and skips five words if it
!             is on; lines 13-15 are three TRANSMITs that save the
!             machine state into SLRBU/SLRMCP; lines 16-18 save the
!             IC; lines 19-26 are EIGHT branch-on-indicator-and-reset
!             instructions, one per I/O and program indicator, each
!             branching to "$.32", i.e. to the very next half word.
!             They are a reset chain, not a dispatch: the fall-through
!             and the taken path are the same place.
!
!             The eight indicators are UNRJ(7), CBJ(8), OP(15),
!             AD(16), EXE(18), USA(17), DS(19) and IF(21), in that
!             order, and the printed low-offset field of each row IS
!             the indicator number halved (7->.3, 8->.4, 15->.7,
!             16->.10, 18->.11, 17->.10, 19->.11, 21->.12 octal,
!             added to the half-word select) with the odd/even bit in
!             the operation byte (C6 for odd, 46 for even).  All
!             eight agree, which is what settles the four round
!             glyphs: see THE NAMES, below.
!
! Lines 27-40 YPREL.  Loads the two-character-set initials through
!             the address SIC planted in it, converts the saved IC to
!             BCD with a count-down loop (lines 30-39, YSFCL2), and
!             stores the result in YPEIC.
!
! Lines 41-50 the exit.  If S L is set, go to YMCPPE on printed
!             p.133; otherwise call SPRIME with the parameter DABEOJ
!             (line 44), reset boundary control (lines 45-46), and
!             write the message on the spool tape through ZSPLPR
!             with the parameters YPPEM and 5.0 (lines 47-50).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE MANUAL DESCRIBES THIS PAGE IN TYPESET PRINT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> C22-6728-1 MCP SYSTEM ANALYSIS GUIDE, "INTERRUPT CONTROL",
! WRITES OUT THIS PAGE'S OWN TABLE ENTRY AND NAMES ITS ROUTINE. <<<
! Found by grepping docs/ocr/ for the names, and it settles more of
! this page than every glyph crop put together.  Quoting:
!
!   "2. Program errors (indicators 6-8, 15-17, 19)"
!   "EKJ, UNRJ, CBJ, OP, AD, USA, DS (6-8, 15-17, 19, program
!    error) ... SIC IN YSFIC ... B TO YFX** (standard fixup; **
!    denotes indicator mnemonic)"
!   "(AX)DD(BU, 32), **X
!    (IQSX)DD(BU,32)  **X"
!   "Control passes to a common fixup routine, YPREFX"
!   "the lower registers are stored in the backup buffer (SLRBU),
!    the program error indicators are cleared, and the EXE and IF
!    indicators are reset"
!   "the level bit (SL) is tested to determine the source of the
!    error"
!   "the IC saved in YSFIC is converted to A8 ... the ABEOJ is
!    primed with control given to the short message routine that
!    writes the error message"
!
! That is typeset, not drum-printed, and it independently gives:
!   * the SPELLINGS YPREFX, YSFIC, SLRBU, SL and ABEOJ;
!   * the EIGHT INDICATORS of lines 19-26 by name and by number,
!     which is what settles their four round glyphs as BCBJZ, BOPZ
!     (not BCPZ), BADZ (not BAOZ) and BUSAZ;
!   * the SHAPE of lines 1-11 -- two entry-mode DDs holding the
!     indicator's own mnemonic, in the 48-character set and the 89-
!     character set -- which is the only outside reading there will
!     ever be of six rows that print no binary at all;
!   * the English for lines 41-50: prime ABEOJ, then the short
!     message routine.  Line 44's parameter is DABEOJ.
! (The manual's template also carries a "VF, XX." ABEX-code row that
! this page does not print.  The locations leave no room for one --
! line 1 at 216440.40, lines 2 and 3 at 216441.00 and 216441.40,
! line 4 at 216442.00, four half words -- so the listing is what is
! transcribed and the difference is recorded, not reconciled.)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE NAMES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> TWO LANDED DECKS ALREADY CARRY THREE OF THIS PAGE'S NAMES AT
! THIS PAGE'S ADDRESSES, WRITTEN BEFORE IT WAS TRANSCRIBED -- AND
! EACH OF THE THREE IS A MERGE COLLISION WAITING FOR WHOEVER WIRES
! THIS PAGE INTO strap/mcp_image.py. <<<  Same value either way, so
! nothing is wrong; but p.110's two SYNs are a FORWARD REFERENCE to
! labels THIS page defines, and p.105 defines DABEOJ outright where
! this deck SYNs it.  Expect duplicate definitions at merge, and
! expect p.110's two SYNs to become removable once this lands.
!   * decks/mcp_bootstrap_p110.strap lines 206-207 SYN "YFXUSA
!     216442.0" and "YFXDS 216444.0" for its own "BD,YFXUSA" and
!     "BD,YFXDS" -- which is exactly where THIS page defines them.
!     The two definitions and the two references now meet, and the
!     !SYM lines below are a real cross-page check, not a reading
!     of this page alone.  The spellings are p.110's.
!   * decks/mcp_bootstrap_p105.strap line 394 defines "DABEOJ SYN,
!     68.0" at 000104.00, the identical symbol, address AND
!     spelling -- O and not C -- that line 44 needs.
! So this deck PREFERS SPELLINGS ANOTHER PAGE ALREADY USES for
! YFXUSA, YFXDS, DABEOJ, and (from p.103/p.110/p.116/p.117) SCOMRG,
! SL, SLRBU, SLRMCP, SICBU, YSFIC, SPRIME and SPRIMR.
!
! EVERY NAME ON THIS PAGE WAS ALSO CHECKED AGAINST THE VOLUME OCR, and
! every one of them is there (docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt and
! ...250-445.txt): YPREFX 4, YPREL 8, YFXUSA 1, YSFCL2 2, SLRBU 25,
! SLRMCP 5, SICBU 4, YSFIC 9, YMFCF 5, YPPEM 3, YMCPIN 1, YPEIC 1,
! YMCPPE 2, SPRIMR 18, SPRIME 19, YSFBCR 3, ZSPLP9 3, ZSPLPR 11.
! That is an index, not a spelling check -- the OCR reads this drum's
! O as C just as the eye does -- but a name with ZERO hits would be
! a reason to look again, and only YFXDS has none (it is defined
! here and, in the part of the volume that is OCR'd, never used).
!
! >>> DABEOJ, LINE 44, IS ALSO SETTLED BY A TYPESET TABLE. <<<  The row
! prints "000104.00 80  ,DABEOJ" and the last-but-one glyph is this
! drum's round one, so the name could be read DABECJ.  Three
! witnesses, none of them ink:
!   * C22-6728 MCP System Analysis Guide, Figure 14 "Major Package
!     Pseudo-Ops", prints "$ABEOJ 68.00".  Decimal 68 IS octal 104,
!     and 68.00 IS this row's value.  The manual is typeset.
!   * The same figure prints "$SCR 68.32", and the volume OCR carries
!     a row "000104.40 80 ... DSCR" -- so the "D" prefix is the
!     listing's name for the pseudo-op word and the pair lines up.
!   * The volume OCR carries, on another page, "000104.00 80  DABEOJ
!     -GO TO END OF JOB" and "SIC,SPRIME -USE ABEOJ", and C22-6728
!     line 1760 reads "CBJ, OP, AD, and USA (6-8, 15-17) result in
!     ABEOJ".  ABEOJ is ABnormal End Of Job.
! That last sentence is doing double duty: it NAMES FOUR OF THIS
! PAGE'S EIGHT INDICATORS in typeset print, which is what settles
! lines 20, 21, 22 and 24 as BCBJZ, BOPZ (not BCPZ), BADZ (not BAOZ)
! and BUSAZ, and corroborates the 6-8/15-17 numbering that the rows'
! own printed offsets gave independently.
!
! >>> YMFCF AND YSFCL2 REST ON INK ALONE, and are the page's two
! soft spots. <<<  Both carry a round glyph that this drum opens.
! YMFCF's address is pinned (the volume OCR has its defining card,
! "216425.00 *  YMFCF  DR(N),(3)", and four more references at
! 216425/216426), but no manual names it and no landed deck uses it,
! so the C-vs-O cannot be decided.  YSFCL2 is defined here and
! referenced only from line 39 of this page, which is the exact
! category docs/transcription_workflow.md warns about: it compiles
! perfectly either way and no test can see it.  Recorded, not fixed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS.  WHAT IS READ AND WHAT IS CONVENTION
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FOUR OF THESE ARE FULLY OBSERVED, because they appear as VFL or
! index operands whose printed address field is a complete 24-bit
! BIT address.  The rest are back-derived from a branch, a SIC or a
! TRANSMIT and are pinned ONLY TO THE HALF WORD -- bit offsets 0-31
! all encode identically, so writing ".0" there is a CONVENTION and
! no !CHECK on this page can test it (docs/transcription_workflow
! .md, "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE", item 1).  Each is marked.
!
! SCOMRG  215001.00  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap line 8
!                    ("S COM RG XW,(8)520000.").  Carried only so
!                    that S L below can be written the way p.103
!                    writes it, exactly as p.128 carries it for S M.
SCOMRG  SYN, (8)215001.0
! SL      215001.04  FULLY OBSERVED.  LANDED, p.103 line 14
!                    ("S L  SYN(BU,1), S COM RG + 0.04").  Lines 12
!                    and 41 are branch-on-bit, whose FIRST half word
!                    is a 24-bit bit address, and both print
!                    215001.04 -- bit 4 is read, not conventional.
SL      SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+0.04
! SLRBU   215324.00  LANDED by the p.116 and p.117 decks.  Line 13
!                    prints 215324.00 and line 14 prints
!                    "SLRBU+16." as 215344.32 -- 16 words on from
!                    215324 is 215344 -- so the WORD is checked
!                    twice and the arithmetic with it.
SLRBU   SYN, (8)215324.0
! SLRMCP  215362.00  LANDED by the p.116 and p.117 decks.  Line 15
!                    prints "SLRMCP+9.0" as 215373.00; 215362+9 is
!                    215373.
SLRMCP  SYN, (8)215362.0
! SICBU   215361.00  LANDED by the p.117 deck.  Line 17 prints
!                    215361.03, whose ".03" is the index field
!                    (register 1, doubled, plus the store bit), not
!                    an address offset.
SICBU   SYN, (8)215361.0
! YSFIC   216604.00  FULLY OBSERVED, and LANDED by the p.110 deck.
!                    Line 32 prints "YSFIC+.18" as 216604.22 --
!                    eighteen decimal bits is .22 octal -- which
!                    reads the word AND the zero bit offset.  The
!                    SPELLING is typeset in C22-6728-1 ("the IC
!                    saved in YSFIC"), twice in each revision.
YSFIC   SYN, (8)216604.0
! YMFCF   216425.00  NEW.  Line 18 prints 216425.03 ($1 index).
!                    Half-word pinned; SPELLING NOT SETTLED, above.
!                    NOT the manual's YMFL or YMFIC: YMFIC is landed
!                    at 216411.40 (p.110) and YMFL is the MACHINE-
!                    error analogue of this page's YPREL.  Grepping
!                    both MCP guides for YMF*/YSF* returns only
!                    YMFL, YMFP, YMFIC and YSFIC -- this name is not
!                    in them.
YMFCF   SYN, (8)216425.0
! YPPEM   216513.00  FULLY OBSERVED.  Line 28 prints "YPPEM+.8" as
!                    216513.10 (eight decimal bits is .10 octal),
!                    which reads the word and the zero offset; line
!                    49 prints the bare symbol as 216513.00.
YPPEM   SYN, (8)216513.0
! YMCPIN  216523.00  FULLY OBSERVED.  Line 29 is a VFL store and
!                    prints 216523.00.
YMCPIN  SYN, (8)216523.0
! YPEIC   216516.40  FULLY OBSERVED.  Line 40 is a VFL store and
!                    prints 216516.40 -- bit 32, read not assumed.
YPEIC   SYN, (8)216516.40
! YMCPPE  216500.40  NEW, and it is this page's forward join.  Line
!                    41 prints 216500.74: octal 74 is the half-word
!                    select (.40) plus branch-on-bit's own .34
!                    operation bits, exactly as printed p.79 line 16
!                    prints 004570.74 0E for "BB1,THEAD,TPENY" with
!                    T PENY at 004570.40.  Half-word pinned.  The
!                    volume OCR puts printed p.133 line 1 at
!                    216500.40 and names it YMCPPE.
YMCPPE  SYN, (8)216500.40
! SPRIMR  215571.00  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap line 288
!                    -- whose own comment already says "pp.132,193
!                    SIC,SPRIMR 215571.00", written before this page
!                    was transcribed.  Half-word pinned.
SPRIMR  SYN, (8)215571.0
! SPRIME  215570.00  LANDED, p.103 line 287, same note.  Line 43
!                    prints 215570.10, the .10 being B's operation
!                    bits.  Half-word pinned.
SPRIME  SYN, (8)215570.0
! DABEOJ  000104.00  NEW.  Line 44 prints 000104.00 80.  Decimal 68,
!                    which C22-6728 Figure 14 prints as "$ABEOJ
!                    68.00".  Half-word pinned; the NAME is settled
!                    (see THE NAMES).
DABEOJ  SYN, (8)104.0
! YSFBCR  215224.00  NEW here.  Line 45 prints 215224.06 ($3 index
!                    doubled).  The volume OCR carries its defining
!                    card, "215224.00+ ... YSFBCR SYN,SBNDRS", and a
!                    second reference at 215224.02.  Half-word
!                    pinned.
YSFBCR  SYN, (8)215224.0
! ZSPLP9  224052.00  NEW.  Line 47 prints 224052.00 80.  The volume
!                    OCR carries three more "SIC,ZSPLP9" rows at the
!                    same address.  Half-word pinned.
ZSPLP9  SYN, (8)224052.0
! ZSPLPR  224046.40  NEW.  Line 48 prints 224046.50: octal 50 is the
!                    half-word select (.40) plus B's .10 operation
!                    bits.  The volume OCR carries five more
!                    "B,ZSPLPR" rows printing the identical 224046.50
!                    00.  Half-word pinned.
ZSPLPR  SYN, (8)224046.40
!
! $MASK (line 15) is the machine's mask register, word 12 -- it is
! in strap/opcodes.py's SPECIAL_REGISTERS and needs no SYN here.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)216440.40
!
        B, YPREFX                     ! line  1
        (AX)DD(BU,32), AD X           ! line  2
        (IQSX)DD(BU,32), AD X         ! line  3
YFXUSA  SIC, YPREL                    ! line  4
        B, YPREFX                     ! line  5
        (AX)DD(BU,32), USAX           ! line  6
        (IQSX)DD(BU,32), USAX         ! line  7
YFXDS   SIC, YPREL                    ! line  8
        B, YPREFX                     ! line  9
        (AX)DD(BU,32), DS X           ! line 10
        (IQSX)DD(BU,32), DS X         ! line 11
YPREFX  BB, SL, $+5.0                 ! line 12
        TI, 16, 3.0, SLRBU            ! line 13
        TI, 13, 19.0, SLRBU+16.       ! line 14
        TI, 1, SLRMCP+9.0, $MASK      ! line 15
        LV, $1, YSFIC                 ! line 16
        SV, $1, SICBU                 ! line 17
        SX, $1, YMFCF                 ! line 18
        BUNRJZ, $.32                  ! line 19
        BCBJZ, $.32                   ! line 20  printed "BCBJ Z"
        BOPZ, $.32                    ! line 21  printed "BOP  Z"
        BADZ, $.32                    ! line 22  printed "BAD  Z"
        BEXEZ, $.32                   ! line 23  printed "BEXE Z"
        BUSAZ, $.32                   ! line 24  printed "BUSAZ "
        BDSZ, $.32                    ! line 25  printed "BDS Z "
        BIFZ, $.32                    ! line 26  printed "BIF Z "
YPREL   L(BU), $                      ! line 27 -LOAD IDENTIFYING INITIALS.
        ST(BU,32), YPPEM+.8, 32       ! line 28
        ST(BU,32), YMCPIN             ! line 29
        LVI, $1, 0                    ! line 30 -CONVERT IC TO BCD
        LCI, $1, 8                    ! line 31
        L(BU,1), YSFIC+.18, 2         ! line 32
        LFI(BU,8), (2)00111011, 8     ! line 33
        LF(BU,18,3), YSFIC, 16        ! line 34
YSFCL2  CT0101(BU,8), 0, 0($1)        ! line 35
        BZRZ, $+1.32                  ! line 36
        LFI(BU,8), (2)00001010, 0($1) ! line 37
        V+I, $1, 4.0                  ! line 38
        CB, $1, YSFCL2                ! line 39
        ST(BU), YPEIC                 ! line 40
        BB1, SL, YMCPPE               ! line 41
        SIC, SPRIMR                   ! line 42
        B, SPRIME                     ! line 43
        , DABEOJ                      ! line 44
        LX, $3, YSFBCR                ! line 45 -RESET BOUNDARY CONTROL.
        SX, $3, 3.0                   ! line 46
        SIC, ZSPLP9                   ! line 47 -WRITE MESSAGE ON SPOOL TAPE.
        B, ZSPLPR                     ! line 48
        , YPPEM                       ! line 49
        , 5.0                         ! line 50
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, AS THE PAGE PRINTS IT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   LINE  LOCATION    BINARY OUTPUT                 NAME     STATEMENT
!    1*   216440.40   216446.10 00                           B,YPREFX
!    2*   216441.00                                          (AX)DD(BU,32), AD X
!    3*   216441.40                                          (IQSX)DD(BU,32), AD X
!    4*   216442.00   216457.40 80                  YFXUSA   SIC,YPREL
!    5*   216442.40   216446.10 00                           B,YPREFX
!    6*   216443.00 *                                        (AX)DD(BU,32), USAX
