!   34*   216465.40   216604.00 80  022310.06 70             LF(BU,18,3),YSFIC,16
!   35*   216466.40   000000.00 80  010000.13 71    YSFCL2   CT0101(BU,8),0,0($1)
!   36*   216467.40   216471.34 C0                           BZRZ,$+1.32
!   37*   216470.00   024000.00 80  410000.06 71             LFI(BU,8),(2)00001010,0($1)
!   38*   216471.00   000004.03 05                           V+I,$1,4.0
!   39*   216471.40   216466.42 48                           CB,$1,YSFCL2
!   40*   216472.00 * 216516.40 80  000000.20 D0             ST(BU),YPEIC
!   41*   216473.00   215001.04 80  216500.74 0E             BB1,SL,YMCPPE
!   42*   216474.00   215571.00 80                           SIC,SPRIMR
!   43*   216474.40   215570.10 00                           B,SPRIME
!   44*   216475.00   000104.00 80                           ,DABEOJ
!   45*   216475.40   215224.06 10                           LX,$3,YSFBCR      -RESET BOUNDARY CONTROL.
!   46*   216476.00   000003.07 10                           SX,$3,3.0
!   47*   216476.40   224052.00 80                           SIC,ZSPLP9        -WRITE MESSAGE ON SPOOL TAPE.
!   48*   216477.00   224046.50 00                           B,ZSPLPR
!   49*   216477.40   216513.00 80                           ,YPPEM
!   50*   216500.00   000005.00 80                           ,5.0
!
! LISTING MARKS.  Every line number carries the ordinary trailing
! asterisk ("1*", "50*"); that is the column, not a mark.  THREE
! rows carry a SECOND asterisk after the LOCATION -- lines 6, 25 and
! 40 -- which is the familiar mark printed pp.3/37/38/39/88/97/98
! and p.104 line 6 also carry.  It changes no compiled bit.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT NO !CHECK ON THIS PAGE CAN SEE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) >>> LINES 2, 3, 6, 7, 10 AND 11 PRINT NO BINARY OUTPUT AT
! ALL, AND NOTHING IN THIS REPOSITORY CAN CHECK THEM IN EITHER
! DIRECTION. <<<  They are entry-mode DDs and the listing leaves the
! column blank, so their CONTENTS are untestable.  THE SIZE IS NO
! HELP EITHER, and this was MEASURED rather than assumed, because
! the obvious hope is that it would be: the three !SYM lines
! YFXUSA/YFXDS/YPREFX sit immediately below these rows, so a datum
! one character short ought to move all three.  It does not.
! Shortening line 2's datum from " AD " to " AD" and re-running the
! verifier leaves YFXUSA at 216442.00, YFXDS at 216444.00 and
! YPREFX at 216446.00 and the page still passes 44 of 44 rows.
!
! The reason is that the emitted width comes from the DATA
! DESCRIPTION -- "(BU,32)" says thirty-two bits -- and not from the
! datum's length, so the datum is padded or truncated to fit and the
! locations below it never move.  (entry_byte_size's own evidence,
! printed p.37's "(AX)DD(BU),03/15/63X", is a dds with NO length,
! which is the case where the characters do set the width.  This
! page is the other case.)
!
! So these six rows rest on the reading of the STATEMENT column
! alone, backed only by C22-6728-1's template and by the padding
! rule being self-consistent across three mnemonics of two
! different lengths.  A WRONG CHARACTER OR A WRONG BLANK HERE WOULD
! BE INVISIBLE FOREVER.  Said plainly so the next reader does not
! mistake this page's "ALL TESTS PASSED" for coverage of them.
!
! THE BLANKS IN THE DATUM ARE READ AS DATA, not formatting
! (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "In entry mode the space after
! the comma is DATA"): the page prints ", AD X", ", USAX" and
! ", DS X", whose data are " AD ", " USA" and " DS " -- four
! characters each, leading blank always, trailing blank on two of
! the three.  (BU,32) names no byte size, which C28-6129 printed
! p.16 makes EIGHT, and four eight-bit characters are the 32 bits
! the locations demand.  Transcribed character for character.
!
! AND THE PADDING IS SELF-CONSISTENT, which is the closest thing to
! a check these six rows can have: C22-6728-1 says the datum is the
! INDICATOR MNEMONIC, and AD is two letters, USA is three, DS is
! two -- so " AD ", " USA" and " DS " are one leading blank plus the
! mnemonic plus however many blanks reach four.  Three rows, three
! different mnemonic lengths, one rule.  That is an argument, not a
! check -- see (1) above for why no check exists -- but it is the
! only independent handle these rows have.
!
! (2) The half-word-pinned externals above: YMCPPE, ZSPLPR, SPRIME,
! SPRIMR, ZSPLP9, DABEOJ, YSFBCR, YMFCF, SLRBU, SLRMCP, SICBU.  Bit
! offsets 0-31 encode identically, so ".0"/".40" is read only as far
! as bit 32.  SL, YSFIC, YPPEM, YMCPIN and YPEIC are NOT in this
! class -- each is a VFL or branch-on-bit operand whose printed
! field is a full 24-bit bit address, so their offsets are read.
!
! (3) The spellings YMFCF and YSFCL2, discussed above.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ASSEMBLER GAP THIS PAGE FOUND
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> STRAP IGNORES BLANKS INSIDE AN OPERATION, AND strap_asm DOES
! NOT. <<<  Lines 20-26 print their operations with blanks inside
! them -- "BCBJ Z", "BOP  Z", "BAD  Z", "BEXE Z", "BUSAZ ", "BDS Z ",
! "BIF Z " -- and all seven are rejected:
!
!     line 38: unknown mnemonic 'BCBJ Z' (not a supported
!     instruction or pseudo-op)
!
! The assembler already ignores blanks inside a SYMBOL ("VF,S ASPUT",
! "SIC,S T IC"), which is the same STRAP rule applied in a different
! column, so this looks like the same gap one code path over.
! TESTED, not assumed: the printed forms were handed to assemble()
! first and the error above is its reply.
!
! The seven rows here are written without the blanks, which is
! bit-identical (the blanks carry no bits), and every printed form
! is recorded in the !CHECK note beside its row.  THE OPERATION
! FIELD IS SIX COLUMNS WIDE and the blanks are padding inside it:
! "BUNRJZ" fills it, "BCBJ Z" puts the Z in column 6, "BUSAZ " in
! column 5.  Measured off the character pitch at 900 dpi, with the
! comma landing in column 7 on five of the eight rows.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SURVEY
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! strap/mcp_survey.py OCR'd this page as 35 rows carrying a
! LOCATION over 216441.CC..216474.CC.  THE PAGE HAS FIFTY, over
! 216440.40..216500.00, and the reading above wins on three
! independent counts: the page header's own "LOCATION 216440" field,
! the card-serial column running ED000050 to ED000099 unbroken, and
! the volume OCR putting printed p.133's first row at 216500.40.
! The survey's own note says its count is a LOWER BOUND.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE DECLARED CHECKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!SYM   YFXUSA   216442.00
!SYM   YFXDS    216444.00
!SYM   YPREFX   216446.00
!SYM   YPREL    216457.40
!SYM   YSFCL2   216466.40
!
